```console
$ redkiln --help
Backlog-as-code: the kernel selects, a harness executes, git records.

Usage: redkiln [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  run      Take the next activity for an item and exit on what it decided
  answer   Answer an open human gate, by the option its question declared
  status   Print the roll-up across every item the store knows
  explain  Print why an item reached the state it is in, from its recorded run
  doctor   Report what is wrong with this repository's configuration and state
  init     Create this repository's `.redkiln/` scaffold
  catalog  Read the activity catalog
  lint     Check a facet registry against a rule and exit by its table

Options:
  -C <PATH>      Act on the repository at this path instead of the working directory
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

```
